# The defaults of a display skin (the skin of the LCD, DisplaySkinCockpit): what an element that does not set an attribute itself gets, written
# like defaults.ymlinc of the main skins, which a display skin does not include (it sets the window frame and a 1920x1080 resolution).
# An element that sets an attribute keeps its own value.

- defaults:
    children:
      # A screen of the display: the size of the LCD, filling it. A screen with a name only, like the main skins: the screen entries
      # without one are no screens, enigma2 reads nothing else of them.
      - screen:
          if name:
            position: "fill"
            resolution: "396,240"

      # A text on the display lies over the background picture of its screen, it has none of its own.
      - widget:
          if render=Label:
            transparent: "1"
